00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:37,760
So I was, I missed the actual launch by a few months just because my account wasn't approved by Apple until then.

91
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,000
So I was ready to go as soon as my account was approved.

92
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:44,240
But I wasn't one of the lucky few who was chosen to be able to do it on day one.

93
00:07:44,560 --> 00:07:49,280
So was the sort of mad rush of people that were just buying random apps.

94
00:07:49,360 --> 00:07:50,960
Is that still a thing once you got in?

95
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:53,760
To some degree.

96
00:07:53,840 --> 00:08:08,560
I mean, I think it was a weird time because the App Store had so few had so few apps that it was even like the number one way that you would get a rush of downloads would be if you submit an update.

97
00:08:08,960 --> 00:08:15,040
Because if you submitted an update, you would show up in the recently changed list in the App Store.

98
00:08:15,440 --> 00:08:20,560
Because they had a chronological list of every time an app was updated, you would get to the top of that list.

99
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:32,320
And it was sort of like at one of the top charts, like top paid, top free and then they had recently updated and recently updated was something that anyone could be in because it wasn't based on how successful you were and so it was this weird game of like right.

100
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:42,640
You know, app review was a long process at that point but it was this thing where you would constantly be wanting and incentivized to always have an update kind of ready to turn around after your last one did.

101
00:08:43,120 --> 00:08:46,640
You know, you get approved, you put another one in the queue because you get this visibility.

102
00:08:46,720 --> 00:08:55,600
And it was only what only worked because the app store was so small that, you know, there were only 100 apps that got an update every day or, you know, a few hundred apps a day overall.

